    "examples": [
      "Come restare? Abbacchiano le noci ¶ Sulle montagne (<i>How can you remain? On the mountains, they are knocking down the walnuts</i>) [1864, Emilio Praga, “Egloga – A Bernardino Zembrini [Eclogue – To Bernardino Zembrini]”, in Penombre, page 11:]\r",
      "Amor par vno ſcherzo alle perſone ¶ Quando non vi s’è drento; e vn legato ¶ Da’ ſuo’ vincigli, vinto dalla pena, ¶ Abbacchiato ne va doue’ nel mena. (<i>Love seems like a joke to people when you're not caught in it; one – tied by Its strings and defeated by the sorrow – disheartened, goes where It leads him.</i>) [1612, Michelangelo Buonarroti the Younger, La Tancia, published 1615, Fourth Act, Seventh Scene, page 98:]"
